<h1>About me</h1>

<section>
  <h2>Brief description</h2>
  <p>
    I'm a Computer Science student at UC San Diego with a growing interest in
    machine learning, deep learning, and full-stack web development.
    I'm drawn to exploring how machine learning can be applied to solving real issues —
    from making everyday tools smarter to tackling problems that matter beyond the tech industry.
    I'm especially interested in how we can design more efficient AI model data centers that are
    <em>environmentally sustainable for all creatures who share this planet.</em>
  </p>
  <p>
    Outside of code, I spend my time speaking for the voiceless: advocating for animal rights
    to protect some of the most vulnerable victims of violence. I have fostered at-risk
    cats when I can, and believe compassion for others belongs at the center of how we build
    the future.
  </p>
</section>

